WEBVTT

00:03.310 --> 00:06.250
<i>Ooh, it's so cold!</i>

00:06.250 --> 00:09.790
It always feels like March weather 
is the hardest to get through.

00:09.790 --> 00:11.310
Sayurin!

00:12.330 --> 00:13.930
Good morning!

00:14.650 --> 00:16.640
You're always so cheery, aren't you?

00:16.640 --> 00:19.290
Huh? Aren't you excited for tomorrow?

00:19.290 --> 00:23.010
Tomorrow? Oh, is tomorrow the 14th?

00:23.340 --> 00:28.420
Yeah, but I don't know... 
A lot of people don't take it that seriously.

00:28.420 --> 00:32.920
You think so? I bet Tsubasa is 
planning on something, though.

00:33.440 --> 00:35.370
It would be nice if he was.

00:36.890 --> 00:37.720
Oh!

00:37.990 --> 00:39.720
Tsuba-cha in the house!

00:39.720 --> 00:41.770
Time for a surprise interview!

00:41.770 --> 00:43.390
Huh? Hey wait!

00:44.690 --> 00:48.730
You mean White Day, right? 
Of course I'm thinking of return gifts.

00:49.010 --> 00:50.910
But I haven't started on anything yet.

00:50.910 --> 00:55.790
Huh? Just like that? I thought I 
could make you more nervous about it.

00:55.790 --> 00:57.470
Huh? Huh?

00:57.470 --> 01:00.790
Well, "surprising" Fuyuki like 
this sure made me nervous.

01:16.130 --> 01:18.800
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:19.640 --> 01:23.010
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:33.960
Super Cute Angels ♥

02:31.170 --> 02:33.960
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:33.960
<b>Boom!</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:33.960
<b>Super Adorable</b>

02:35.310 --> 02:36.310
Shiki!

02:38.470 --> 02:43.140
<b>Episode 9:
Lake Abashiri Is Super Relaxing</b>

02:38.470 --> 02:43.140
<b>Episode 9:
Lake Abashiri Is Super Relaxing</b>

02:38.810 --> 02:40.080
What's wrong, Matsuo-kun?

02:40.080 --> 02:42.070
Sorry. Got a sec?

02:42.070 --> 02:43.680
Uh, sure.

02:44.250 --> 02:46.150
You know what day tomorrow is, right?

02:46.640 --> 02:50.810
Uh, wait. Are you talking about White Day?

02:50.810 --> 02:52.940
Yeah! Exactly!

02:52.940 --> 02:56.150
I wanted to ask your advice about that.

02:57.860 --> 03:00.330
I really do feel bad about it.

03:00.860 --> 03:04.160
And so you want to apologize 
to Fuyuki-san and Akino-san?

03:04.160 --> 03:08.620
Yeah. What I said to them was really awful.

03:08.620 --> 03:12.000
What a total letdown.

03:12.420 --> 03:15.550
I really didn't mean anything by that,

03:15.550 --> 03:18.420
but I thought about it later, 
and she did give me chocolate.

03:18.420 --> 03:20.860
I realized I'd been a total jerk.

03:22.010 --> 03:25.570
I haven't really spent time 
with Fuyumina since then

03:25.570 --> 03:29.020
and I think Akino-san 
must really hate me now.

03:29.490 --> 03:31.690
Next time you talk to Fuyuki like that,

03:31.970 --> 03:33.770
I'm literally gonna pound you.

03:34.120 --> 03:37.210
So I thought I could give them 
a return gift on White Day

03:37.210 --> 03:39.430
and apologize to them both at the same time.

03:39.950 --> 03:44.230
But what do you think I should say? 
I really need your advice, Shiki!

03:44.230 --> 03:45.570
Okay, well...

03:45.570 --> 03:50.540
Why not just give a proper apology and 
tell them that you want to stay friends?

03:50.540 --> 03:51.210
Huh?

03:51.620 --> 03:57.060
I doubt Fuyuki-san is still upset about it. 
I'm sure she wants to stay friends with you.

03:57.060 --> 04:00.630
And if Akino-san sees you 
apologizing to Fuyuki-san,

04:00.630 --> 04:02.800
that will probably be enough for her.

04:04.240 --> 04:05.300
Shiki...

04:05.930 --> 04:07.200
Are you a pro or something?

04:07.200 --> 04:09.060
A pro? At what?

04:09.060 --> 04:11.220
Cool. Shiki, thank you!

04:11.220 --> 04:13.600
M'kay, then I'll definitely 
apologize tomorrow.

04:13.600 --> 04:17.020
Okay! I'm really glad I was able to help.

04:18.580 --> 04:20.570
All right. Me, too.

04:22.500 --> 04:23.780
Grandma?

04:24.880 --> 04:26.860
What is it, Tsubasa-chan?

04:28.420 --> 04:30.410
Can I ask for your help with something?

04:32.790 --> 04:35.040
<b>Hokkaido Flour</b>

04:32.790 --> 04:35.040
<b>Mitsuba Milk</b>

04:35.040 --> 04:37.260
Is this really all we need?

04:37.260 --> 04:42.090
I do add butter occasionally, 
but you always preferred it without.

04:42.090 --> 04:44.550
That's right! I remember now.

04:44.550 --> 04:47.260
However, this White Day...

04:47.260 --> 04:49.570
We never had anything like that in the past.

04:49.570 --> 04:51.770
When you want to express 
your gratitude to someone,

04:52.230 --> 04:54.320
if you do it formally, it can 
get a little awkward sometimes,

04:54.320 --> 04:56.400
so it's nice to have an excuse like this.

04:58.060 --> 05:03.280
Everyone wants to make the people 
dear to them happy, after all.

05:05.780 --> 05:09.440
That's true. 
You're absolutely right, Tsubasa-chan.

05:11.740 --> 05:13.870
Fuyumina... Sorry!

05:14.500 --> 05:18.220
I said some nasty stuff to you on 
Valentine's Day and I'm really sorry!

05:18.220 --> 05:19.790
I really regret it!

05:20.140 --> 05:24.990
And so, as thanks and as an apology, 
here's an onion pie from Uzenya.

05:24.990 --> 05:28.530
What? Seriously? I love these!

05:28.530 --> 05:31.890
I'd totally forgotten about 
that anyway. Hilarious!

05:32.960 --> 05:34.000
Mat-tsun.

05:34.880 --> 05:38.210
Thanks, okay? Let's stay pals, okay?

05:39.260 --> 05:42.360
Fuyumina!

05:44.000 --> 05:45.970
What? Is somebody there?

05:47.640 --> 05:50.780
Sorry, Matsuo-kun. 
I was just a little worried.

05:50.780 --> 05:53.090
Akino-san, you aren't mad anymore, are you?

05:53.090 --> 05:56.910
No. If Fuyuki is cool with it, so am I.

05:56.910 --> 05:59.750
Ah. Akino-san, here's one for you.

05:59.750 --> 06:00.650
For me?

06:01.050 --> 06:02.290
Of course!

06:02.880 --> 06:04.450
Oh, right. Me, too.

06:04.840 --> 06:06.470
As thanks for Valentine's Day.

06:06.470 --> 06:09.090
Wow, thanks!

06:09.320 --> 06:12.470
This is the first time I've ever made sweets.

06:12.470 --> 06:13.880
Are they... cookies?

06:13.880 --> 06:15.190
Or rice crackers?

06:15.190 --> 06:17.080
My grandma used to make these for me.

06:17.080 --> 06:20.020
They're my very favorite. 
Milk senbei rice crackers.

06:20.280 --> 06:24.190
I thought this would be a great chance 
to share my favorite sweets with you.

06:24.190 --> 06:24.940
Is that kind of weird?

06:24.940 --> 06:27.210
No! I'm super happy!

06:27.210 --> 06:29.070
You would do something this nice.

06:29.870 --> 06:31.490
What a great guy.

06:32.040 --> 06:34.090
What can I do to show you my gratitude?!

06:34.090 --> 06:36.580
Huh? You don't need to do anything!

06:36.580 --> 06:39.370
Is there anything you want? 
Something you're into right now?

06:39.620 --> 06:41.460
No, not really...

06:41.670 --> 06:44.610
Then try to think of something. I will, too.

06:44.610 --> 06:46.340
Um, okay.

06:49.700 --> 06:53.170
The milk senbei were really popular. 
Everyone said they were delicious.

06:53.170 --> 06:55.680
Is that right? I'm glad to hear that.

06:55.680 --> 06:58.910
Fuyuki-san said she wanted 
to try making them herself,

06:58.910 --> 07:00.980
so she wanted to ask you for the recipe.

07:01.680 --> 07:03.120
Very well.

07:03.120 --> 07:05.940
I'll write it down for her later.

07:09.070 --> 07:10.860
Milk Senbei Recipe
Ingredients (for 18 crackers)
Eggs - 1
Sugar - 45 Grams
Flour - 80 Grams
Milk - 20cc
1. Heat oven to 170 degrees.
2. In a bowl,

07:11.240 --> 07:14.300
Here is my grandma's recipe. There.

07:14.690 --> 07:15.270
Huh?

07:15.880 --> 07:17.140
From Matsuo-kun?

07:17.140 --> 07:18.690
<b>You free on Sunday?</b>

07:18.690 --> 07:20.340
<b>Wanna go smelt fishing?</b>

07:20.680 --> 07:22.170
<b>As thanks for today.</b>

07:22.170 --> 07:23.580
<b>My dad's coming too.</b>

07:24.080 --> 07:27.660
Smelt fishing? I've never tried that before.

07:28.750 --> 07:30.670
<b>Is it okay if I'm a total beginner?</b>

07:31.430 --> 07:32.800
<b>Sure!</b>

07:34.740 --> 07:37.310
<b>Abashiri River System First-Class Waterway
Lake Abashiri</b>

07:37.950 --> 07:41.370
<i>Wow! So this is Lake Abashiri.</i>

07:41.370 --> 07:43.540
We're here! Smelt fishing!

07:43.540 --> 07:46.590
This is my first time, so I'm really excited!

07:46.590 --> 07:48.360
That looks like a good spot over there.

07:48.690 --> 07:51.530
'Kay, Dad, we're gonna head that way.

07:51.530 --> 07:53.400
Sure. Good luck.

07:53.400 --> 07:55.870
Thank you very much! We'll do our best!

07:56.320 --> 08:01.200
The fishing season is almost over, so let's 
have fun and catch everything we can!

08:01.200 --> 08:01.970
Yeah!

08:02.350 --> 08:03.580
What?

08:05.360 --> 08:08.710
Tsubasa and Mat-tsun? Why are you guys here?

08:08.710 --> 08:10.010
Fuyuki-san?

08:08.710 --> 08:10.010
Fuyumina?

08:10.010 --> 08:12.380
Seriously? What a surprise!

08:12.380 --> 08:14.530
I invited Shiki to come.

08:14.530 --> 08:15.890
But why are you here?

08:15.890 --> 08:20.400
My dad loves fishing. 
The whole family comes every year.

08:20.400 --> 08:21.810
Oh, really?

08:25.260 --> 08:28.730
Dad and them didn't catch a thing, 
so they moved to a different spot.

08:28.730 --> 08:32.640
I'm bored out of my mind and was 
about to go back to the car.

08:32.640 --> 08:35.280
'Kay, then why don't you 
fish with us, Fuyumina?

08:35.280 --> 08:36.740
Huh? Can I?

08:36.740 --> 08:38.280
That's okay with you, right?

08:38.630 --> 08:39.910
Of course!

08:42.390 --> 08:45.290
First, you cut a hole, like this.

08:45.290 --> 08:47.040
I've seen this on TV before!

08:47.040 --> 08:49.920
It's tough 'cause it takes a lot of strength.

08:49.920 --> 08:55.140
And then seats. There's no way 
you could do this standing.

08:55.140 --> 09:00.310
And the tent... Well, the weather's good 
and there's no wind, so maybe later.

09:00.310 --> 09:01.710
Here. Your rod.

09:01.870 --> 09:04.500
Red Maggots

09:02.080 --> 09:03.560
Shiki, can you handle bait?

09:03.560 --> 09:04.720
Um...

09:04.720 --> 09:07.610
No problem. I'll do it for now.

09:07.610 --> 09:10.320
If you wanna try after you 
get used to it, just say so.

09:10.880 --> 09:12.040
When you're ready,

09:12.040 --> 09:15.290
drop the line in the hole until the 
weight hits the bottom of the lake.

09:15.290 --> 09:17.780
Then gently lift up and down to attract fish.

09:17.780 --> 09:21.200
Smelt like to hang around 
the bottom of the lake.

09:21.850 --> 09:23.720
Wow, Matsuo-kun!

09:23.720 --> 09:25.490
You're so dependable!

09:25.490 --> 09:28.610
I always made Dad put the bait on mine!

09:28.610 --> 09:29.880
I got you covered!

09:30.360 --> 09:32.670
We're having a smelt party today!

09:32.670 --> 09:34.420
Yeah!

09:45.350 --> 09:46.850
<b>One Hour Later</b>

09:55.280 --> 09:56.880
We haven't caught a thing.

09:56.880 --> 10:00.910
When you get a bite, the rods should 
start wiggling. But they haven't at all.

10:00.910 --> 10:04.790
B-But part of the fun of 
fishing is the waiting, right?

10:04.790 --> 10:07.710
Shiki is so considerate, 
it makes me feel all warm inside!

10:08.350 --> 10:10.820
I'll go see how my dad is doing.

10:11.250 --> 10:13.990
This spot might have been a dud.

10:13.990 --> 10:15.980
Yeah, all right.

10:15.980 --> 10:18.080
Okay! We'll wait here!

10:18.080 --> 10:18.630
Yeah!

10:19.520 --> 10:23.370
Wouldn't it be hilarious if 
we caught a bunch while he's gone?

10:23.370 --> 10:24.260
Yeah.

10:28.000 --> 10:29.750
I don't think that's happening, though.

10:29.750 --> 10:32.150
They aren't taking the bait at all.

10:48.360 --> 10:51.050
Fuyuki-san, aren't you bored?

10:51.050 --> 10:53.540
Huh? No, I'm not bored.

10:54.120 --> 10:57.070
Really? That's good.

10:57.070 --> 10:58.400
But I mean,

10:58.800 --> 11:02.330
it's been a long time since 
we've been left alone like this.

11:02.800 --> 11:05.100
Isn't that right, Tsubacha-kun?

11:05.100 --> 11:08.080
Uh, yeah. You might be right.

11:09.690 --> 11:13.380
<i>We've spent so much time together 
I thought I was getting used to it,</i>

11:13.380 --> 11:15.110
<i>but she's still too strong for me!</i>

11:15.110 --> 11:17.690
It'd be weird to sit here 
without talking while we wait,

11:17.690 --> 11:19.960
so you wanna watch a video or something?

11:19.960 --> 11:22.990
Huh? Yeah, sounds good. 
Let's watch something.

11:22.990 --> 11:25.490
These are, like, super crazy!

11:25.700 --> 11:27.850
Oh. Makeup videos?

11:27.850 --> 11:31.050
Yeah! There's this influencer 
I've been following recently.

11:31.050 --> 11:34.190
Her makeup skills are so godly, 
it's like her models become different people!

11:33.000 --> 11:36.000
<b>Makeup</b>

11:33.000 --> 11:36.000
<b>Featured        Users             Videos        Music                          {missing}</b>

11:33.000 --> 11:36.000
<b>My morning routine
#routine</b>

11:33.000 --> 11:36.000
<b>Moisturizing tips for hot guys
#makeup #hotguys</b>

11:34.190 --> 11:36.000
There are even some for men's makeup.

11:36.000 --> 11:39.590
I wanna get as good as she is at makeup!

11:39.950 --> 11:44.550
I think your makeup always looks 
natural and is really lovely.

11:45.550 --> 11:48.430
Oh, have I been dazzling you 
with my looks this whole time?

11:48.430 --> 11:50.260
You think I look "lovely"?

11:50.260 --> 11:52.880
No, you're wrong! I mean, you're not wrong!

11:52.880 --> 11:54.810
But, the makeup! 
I'm talking about your makeup!

11:55.710 --> 11:58.410
That said, I don't know much about makeup,

11:58.410 --> 12:01.900
so I'm sure there are a lot of 
techniques I don't know about.

12:01.900 --> 12:06.240
But you know so much about it, and 
you're always studying. That's amazing!

12:06.240 --> 12:10.080
I guess it takes a lot of effort 
to look that pretty or cute.

12:12.560 --> 12:13.310
Yeah.

12:14.010 --> 12:18.840
But it's not just for me. 
I want to make everyone look pretty.

12:19.210 --> 12:20.160
Everyone?

12:21.790 --> 12:25.480
I want to get a whole lot better at makeup

12:25.480 --> 12:27.930
and start studying everything 
I can about beauty.

12:28.710 --> 12:32.130
It would be great if I could study abroad...

12:34.060 --> 12:36.790
Th-That's still just a dream, though!

12:36.790 --> 12:40.480
You've put so much thought into it... 
You're amazing, Fuyuki-san!

12:40.940 --> 12:45.070
It's like you see beauty and 
makeup on a whole other level!

12:55.360 --> 12:56.170
Anyway,

12:56.500 --> 12:59.300
do you ever use wax or anything, Tsubasa?

12:59.300 --> 13:00.640
Huh? Me?

13:00.640 --> 13:02.590
No, I never have.

13:02.590 --> 13:06.890
You've got great features, so a little 
effort there could totally transform you!

13:07.470 --> 13:11.220
I mean, look at how pretty your skin is.

13:11.220 --> 13:12.270
<i>She's so close!</i>

13:12.270 --> 13:14.230
I totally want to do your makeup.

13:14.230 --> 13:15.660
I-I don't though!

13:15.660 --> 13:16.940
No, that's no good.

13:16.940 --> 13:21.560
I mean, you go outside without using 
any toner or moisturizer, right?

13:21.560 --> 13:23.000
Right.

13:23.000 --> 13:27.160
That's just cray-cray when it's 
this cold and dry outside.

13:27.650 --> 13:32.140
At least use some lip balm, okay? 
I'll let you borrow mine.

13:32.140 --> 13:34.580
It smells great and will make 
your lips look full and shiny.

13:34.580 --> 13:36.970
Borrow? Yours?

13:36.970 --> 13:39.400
If not, your lips are 
gonna get dry and cracked.

13:39.400 --> 13:42.190
I'll put it on, so pucker up, okay?

13:42.190 --> 13:44.210
Fuyuki-san, this is a little too...

13:44.210 --> 13:47.120
<i>It's an ultra high-level indirect kiss!</i>

13:47.120 --> 13:47.800
Here, now.

13:54.970 --> 13:59.080
<i>Fuyuki-san's lips... 
They do look full and shiny.</i>

13:59.630 --> 14:02.570
<i>And it does have a subtle but nice fragrance.</i>

14:04.160 --> 14:10.410
<i>Right here, right now, if Fuyuki-san 
puts the lip balm she uses on my lips,</i>

14:11.000 --> 14:12.980
<i>that's basically an actual...!</i>

14:20.510 --> 14:21.570
Hey!

14:22.630 --> 14:25.070
Shiki! Fuyumina!

14:25.070 --> 14:27.520
My dad caught tons of fish!

14:27.520 --> 14:32.000
We should find a new spot, get a bunch 
of fish, and then fry them as tempura!

14:32.000 --> 14:35.430
I love smelt tempura! 
Let's go! Let's go!

14:38.250 --> 14:42.270
<i>Another second and Fuyuki-san would've 
fished my soul right out of my body!</i>

14:42.550 --> 14:43.910
We're going, Shiki!

14:43.910 --> 14:47.030
<i>You saved me! Thank you, Matsuo-kun!</i>

14:50.120 --> 14:51.950
I finally caught some!

14:51.950 --> 14:54.370
Me, too! I caught some! I'm so happy!

14:54.620 --> 14:57.290
Looks like changing spots was the right move!

14:58.790 --> 15:00.040
Whoa!

15:00.040 --> 15:02.280
It looks super delicious!

15:02.280 --> 15:04.040
Let's eat while they're hot.

15:04.490 --> 15:06.900
I've never had smelt before!

15:07.680 --> 15:10.630
Oh, yum!

15:11.300 --> 15:12.800
Thank you for the food.

15:14.050 --> 15:16.230
The outside is crunchy batter,

15:16.230 --> 15:19.260
but the inside is filled with 
the hot and chewy smelt flavor!

15:19.260 --> 15:22.720
And this delicious aroma filling my nose!

15:22.720 --> 15:25.460
It's the flavor of the great outdoors!

15:25.460 --> 15:29.990
Thank you, smelt! Thank you, Hokkaido!

15:30.240 --> 15:32.360
He looks like he's lovin' every bite!

15:32.360 --> 15:36.660
Tsubasa is like that. He makes 
food look really delicious.

15:36.660 --> 15:37.270
Oh.

15:37.800 --> 15:41.000
Shiki, my mom made some rice balls. 
Try one! They're delicious.

15:41.680 --> 15:43.380
Seasoned rice and scallops!

15:43.940 --> 15:45.440
Thank you!

15:47.740 --> 15:51.160
<i>Even cold, the rice is chewy 
and the shellfish are plump!</i>

15:51.160 --> 15:54.170
<i>And together with the fragrance of 
the scorched rice filling my mouth,</i>

15:54.170 --> 15:55.800
<i>this is delicious!</i>

15:56.250 --> 16:00.640
<i>This combination of piping hot 
smelt tempura and rice balls is</i>

16:00.870 --> 16:03.650
absolutely perfect!

16:06.090 --> 16:07.570
I can totally relate!

16:07.570 --> 16:12.400
<b>Kitami Butter</b>

16:07.800 --> 16:12.400
The Matsuo family recipe calls for melting 
some butter in the scallop broth.

16:12.400 --> 16:14.510
This is so good, Matsuo-kun!

16:14.510 --> 16:16.190
Gourmet rice balls!

16:16.820 --> 16:19.660
Oh! Shiki's line is getting tugged again!

16:20.180 --> 16:21.710
You're right!

16:21.710 --> 16:24.180
Tsubasa, go get 'em!

16:25.050 --> 16:29.050
<i>My first time smelt fishing was totally fun!</i>

16:31.220 --> 16:32.050
<i>But...</i>

16:34.330 --> 16:36.890
<i>I also totally caught a cold.</i>

16:38.150 --> 16:41.300
<i>I never should have been goofing 
around with my jacket off.</i>

16:46.440 --> 16:48.350
<b>1 new message from Akino-san</b>

16:46.970 --> 16:48.350
It's from Akino-san.

16:48.350 --> 16:51.410
<b>Matsuo told me you caught 
a cold. Are you okay?</b>

16:51.410 --> 16:55.530
<b>It actually isn't that bad so I'm 
okay! Sorry if I made you worry.</b>

16:55.530 --> 16:58.770
<b>No problem! Stay warm and rest up.</b>

16:58.770 --> 17:00.810
<b>When you're better, let's play more games.</b>

17:01.010 --> 17:02.040
<b>Let's hang out ba-dump!</b>

17:02.370 --> 17:04.850
<i>Thank you, Akino-san.</i>

17:04.850 --> 17:05.960
Tsubasa-chan?

17:09.610 --> 17:10.960
How are you feeling?

17:10.960 --> 17:13.620
I think I'm a little better 
than I was this morning.

17:13.620 --> 17:17.080
Really? I made some rice 
porridge so try to eat it.

17:17.080 --> 17:18.150
I will.

17:18.150 --> 17:20.680
Also, this came from the 
young lady next door.

17:20.940 --> 17:22.980
From Natsukawa-senpai?

17:22.980 --> 17:26.120
She just came over with 
the neighborhood bulletin.

17:26.120 --> 17:30.820
When I told her about you, she went 
all the way back home to get this.

17:30.820 --> 17:38.070
To Shiki-kun,
I realize it isn't much,
but please drink this and stay hydrated.
Take care of yourself. Natsukawa

17:31.230 --> 17:32.550
<i>To Shiki-kun,</i>

17:32.550 --> 17:36.060
<i>I realize it isn't much, but please 
drink this and stay hydrated.</i>

17:36.470 --> 17:37.570
<i>Take care of yourself.</i>

17:38.070 --> 17:42.450
She did? Everyone's so kind, 
it makes me feel warm inside.

17:42.670 --> 17:45.600
Is it all right if I step 
out to run some errands?

17:45.600 --> 17:48.960
Ah, yes. I'll be fine. Stay safe.

17:48.960 --> 17:51.310
Please try to get some rest.

17:59.930 --> 18:03.890
Th-This is bad. It's getting a lot worse.

18:04.360 --> 18:07.700
I never expected to end up sick 
with spring just around the corner.

18:08.100 --> 18:11.900
The worst part is that I feel really lonely.

18:12.360 --> 18:14.400
I always thought I was used to being alone,

18:15.130 --> 18:17.420
but today I need somebody...

18:17.420 --> 18:18.320
Tsubasa!

18:19.780 --> 18:22.700
How's your cold? I came to check on you.

18:23.950 --> 18:25.260
Fuyuki-san!

18:25.260 --> 18:28.740
Don't you dare sit up! You need to lie still!

18:29.240 --> 18:31.430
Uh, okay.

18:31.920 --> 18:36.190
Your granny told me that you shouldn't 
get too much stimulation, okay?

18:37.500 --> 18:39.590
I bumped into her nearby.

18:39.590 --> 18:44.260
She seemed worried about you, so I 
promised to look after you for a while.

18:44.480 --> 18:48.940
<i>The fact that you're here in my room 
is already way too stimulating!</i>

18:48.940 --> 18:50.690
Tsubasa, do you mind?

19:01.230 --> 19:02.040
<i>Wha—!</i>

19:02.740 --> 19:05.200
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

19:05.200 --> 19:07.080
That's a nasty cough.

19:07.080 --> 19:10.540
Your nose is stuffed up. 
And your fever is worse than I thought.

19:11.380 --> 19:12.530
Just a minute.

19:12.880 --> 19:15.300
<b>Aroma of the North
Kitami Peppermint Candy</b>

19:13.340 --> 19:15.300
You should have one of these.

19:15.660 --> 19:16.880
Uh, candy?

19:16.880 --> 19:20.760
Yeah! It's a mint candy made 
with peppermint from Kitami.

19:20.760 --> 19:22.020
It's really soothing.

19:22.020 --> 19:24.640
I've never seen it before.

19:24.640 --> 19:28.560
I'll have one when I get a sore throat 
or when I want to refresh my mind.

19:31.650 --> 19:35.080
<i>Ah. The mint flavor is really gentle.</i>

19:35.510 --> 19:37.780
<i>It's a nice balance of refreshing and sweet.</i>

19:38.460 --> 19:40.650
It feels a little easier to breathe now.

19:40.650 --> 19:42.290
Oh, good!

19:42.290 --> 19:46.810
But I'm sure it was my fault that you 
caught a cold in the first place, Tsubasa.

19:46.810 --> 19:49.920
That isn't true! 
I should've been more careful.

19:49.920 --> 19:52.790
No, it wasn't your fault.

19:52.790 --> 19:57.520
When we were fishing, I kept pushing you 
to try one more time, and one more time...

19:57.900 --> 20:01.840
So... I will take full responsibility 
for that and service you today!

20:01.840 --> 20:03.940
<i>Ser-Service me?</i>

20:05.220 --> 20:08.390
I'll do anything you say, Tsubasa!

20:10.040 --> 20:12.210
<i>A-Anything?</i>

20:13.300 --> 20:16.420
Um, I think I need to lie down.

20:16.810 --> 20:18.230
Are you okay?

20:19.110 --> 20:22.490
Not sure. Feels like the room is spinning.

20:22.790 --> 20:25.290
Is there anything you want me to do?

20:25.290 --> 20:26.780
I'll do anything!

20:26.780 --> 20:29.950
<i>Something I want her to do?</i>

20:30.270 --> 20:33.960
<i>Oh, no. I can't think of anything right now.</i>

20:33.960 --> 20:36.830
Tsubasa, your face is bright red!

20:38.720 --> 20:41.100
<i>Oh. That's it.</i>

20:42.910 --> 20:44.180
Fuyuki-san.

20:44.460 --> 20:45.180
What is it?

20:46.650 --> 20:49.140
I want you to stay by my side.

20:56.970 --> 20:57.810
Sure.

21:13.600 --> 21:17.040
I feel a hundred percent better!

21:17.250 --> 21:20.170
I think the mint candies 
Fuyuki-san gave me helped.

21:20.620 --> 21:22.090
I should thank her.

21:22.460 --> 21:25.190
<b>Fuyuki-san! I'm feeling much better now!</b>

21:25.190 --> 21:28.900
<b>And my throat doesn't hurt! 
I think those candies helped.</b>

21:28.900 --> 21:33.150
<b>Good morning! I know, right? 
Peppermint candy is godly!</b>

21:33.150 --> 21:36.020
<b>But I'm seriously happy 
you're feeling better!</b>

21:37.520 --> 21:41.050
<b>Thank you! And I was really happy 
when you visited yesterday.</b>

21:42.070 --> 21:46.780
<b>It's just, I was asleep before I knew it. 
Didn't we talk about something?</b>

21:50.470 --> 21:52.710
<b>No, we didn't really talk about anything.</b>

21:52.710 --> 21:55.330
<b>You fell straight asleep like a little baby.</b>

21:55.330 --> 21:56.890
A little baby?

21:57.490 --> 22:00.300
<i>Oh, okay. But then...</i>

22:02.440 --> 22:06.880
I thought... it felt like 
we were holding hands.

22:07.710 --> 22:09.440
<i>Did I imagine it?</i>

22:18.350 --> 22:20.360
Thank you! And I was really happy
when you visited yesterday.

It's just, I was asleep before I knew it.
Didn't we talk about something?

No, we didn't really talk about anything!
You fell straight asleep like a little baby.

22:21.880 --> 22:23.190
<i>It would be great...</i>

22:24.640 --> 22:28.500
<i>if we could stay together like this forever.</i>
